      "heading": "Which online therapy platforms take insurance?",
      "body": "<p><strong>All three platforms we cover now work with insurance, but in different ways. Talkspace is built around it - in-network with many major commercial plans, Medicare, TRICARE and employer assistance programs, for therapy and psychiatry alike. betterhelp, for years the self-pay holdout, now accepts insurance through a coverage check at signup. headspace accepts insurance for its therapy service, while its meditation app remains a consumer subscription.</strong> The table below is the comparison in one place; the three sections after it go platform by platform.</p>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Platform</th><th>Insurance accepted?</th><th>Plans named</th><th>Typical cost with coverage</th><th>Psychiatry covered?</th><th>Self-pay fallback</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Talkspace</td><td>Yes - in-network</td><td>Aetna, Cigna, Optum, Anthem plans, Medicare, TRICARE, many EAPs</td><td>Copay typically $0 to $30; $0 for many members</td><td>Yes</td><td>$69 to $109 per week; psychiatry $299 then $175</td></tr>\n<tr><td>betterhelp</td><td>Yes - coverage check at signup</td><td>Not listed publicly; checked per member</td><td>Copays cited from around $23 per session</td><td>No psychiatry offered</td><td>Subscription quoted at signup; financial-aid questionnaire</td></tr>\n<tr><td>headspace (therapy service)</td><td>Yes - coverage check on its site</td><td>Checked per member</td><td>Depends on plan</td><td>No psychiatry offered</td><td>Not verified by us at time of writing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>headspace (meditation app)</td><td>No - consumer subscription</td><td>n/a</td><td>n/a</td><td>n/a</td><td>HSA/FSA eligible; may be included in employer benefits</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Two practical notes. First, \"accepts insurance\" always means specific plans; the only way to know yours is covered is the platform's own check. Second, insurance billing on these platforms is usually per live session, so if your interest is a messaging-heavy plan, ask what the insurer is billed for. Our <a href=\"/best-online-therapy-with-insurance\">insurance-friendly platforms comparison</a> ranks the three on this dimension, and our <a href=\"/articles/online-therapy-that-takes-insurance\">shorter insurance guide</a> is the quick version of this page.</p>"
